PR #1063: the AMD asserted chacha20-poly1305/key cell, by disassembly, and the staged A/B pair 3.

crypto_parity (asserted build, x86_64-unknown-toyos) built at the metal revisions 190f3b164 (base) and
9a5d4fad5 (head), and at 8ca3a2e07 / 41977c528 / ba42889cd (pair 3's base and head). rowdiff.txt: the row's
three functions, the loop body, SealingKey::chacha20_poly1305 and drop_glue<aead::Key> (Secret's wipe inlined),
per build: address, address mod 64, size, instruction count and a hash with addresses taken out.

- The instructions are identical in base and head. loop.diff shows that the loop bodies differ only in symbol
  hash suffixes and label comments. The constructor and the drop hash the same.
- The layout changed: the constructor moved from 0xc9180 (mod 64 = 0) to 0xf5360 (mod 64 = 32). The loop and
  the drop keep their alignment, at other addresses.
- The builds are deterministic per source: 9a5d4fad5, 41977c528 and ba42889cd give the same addresses and code,
  and so do 190f3b164 and 8ca3a2e07. So AMD head-1 (6.0 ns) and head-2 (6.9 ns) ran the same code at the same
  addresses.
